WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.605 --> 00:00:08.588
A ship in this game is a hull, four parts, a sea crystal and a crew. The Ship tab is all five at once.

2
00:00:14.876 --> 00:00:20.316
Each slot takes the best part you already hold, or one you pick yourself.

3
00:00:20.316 --> 00:00:26.187
Your Sailing Mastery counts toward speed as well, so it is a number you type in.

4
00:00:29.806 --> 00:00:32.997
And every figure on the card moves with it.

5
00:00:32.997 --> 00:00:39.058
The crew is the part nobody enjoys entering. Eighteen sailors, four growths each.

6
00:00:39.058 --> 00:00:48.277
It is also the part that cannot be estimated: a levelled sailor's real rolls are what make the speed the game's, rather than a guess.

7
00:00:48.277 --> 00:00:52.228
So it reads them off the screenshots you already took.

8
00:00:56.146 --> 00:01:00.844
Drop in the game's own Manage Sailors window, one sailor a shot.

9
00:01:00.844 --> 00:01:05.809
The reading happens here in the browser. The files never leave the machine.

10
00:01:05.809 --> 00:01:10.107
It works through them, and comes back with a table rather than a roster,

11
00:01:10.107 --> 00:01:15.316
because a scan that misreads a level should cost you a glance, not a crew.

12
00:01:26.972 --> 00:01:31.157
Check them against the game, and take the ones that are right.

13
00:01:34.945 --> 00:01:39.664
A whole fit-out can be kept under a name, and switched between.

14
00:01:44.852 --> 00:01:50.147
And the lot of it copies as a link, if someone asks what you are sailing.

15
00:01:52.513 --> 00:01:58.341
That is your ship: every number on it either yours, or read off your own screen.
